{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"The clean directory returns exit code 0, and the external link is skipped. Everything is working normally. I'll summarize concisely.\n","seq":618,"t":59911,"text":"\n\nDone.\n\n**`linkcheck.py`** — stdlib only (`os`, `re`, `sys`). It walks the given directory (default `.`) for `.md` files, extracts inline Markdown links with a regex, and for each link:\n- skips external targets (any `scheme:` like `http:`, `mailto:`) and pure anchors (`#...`) via `local_target()`\n- strips `<...>` wrappers, trailing `\"title\"` parts, and `#anchor` suffixes\n- resolves the path relative to the file's directory and checks existence\n\nBroken links print as `file:line: target`; exit code is 1 if any were found, 0 otherwise.\n\n**`docs/`** — `a.md`, `b.md`, `c.md` all link to each other; `c.md` line 3 links to nonexistent `missing.md`.\n\nRun:\n```\n$ python3 linkcheck.py docs\ndocs/c.md:3: missing.md\nexit: 1\n```\n\nI also verified the success path: a temp dir with only valid local links (plus an `https://` link) produced no output and exit 0.\n\nTo test further: run against a directory with no `.md` files (expect exit 0), and add a link with a title, e.g. `[x](b.md \"B\")`, to confirm title stripping works.\n\n-- checked against AGENTS.md","timings":{"cache_n":5120,"draft_n":686,"draft_n_accepted":234,"predicted_ms":3490.0,"predicted_n":332,"prompt_ms":380.0,"prompt_n":282},"to_request":516,"usage":{"cached_tokens":5120,"completion_tokens":332,"prompt_tokens":5402}}
